{"c":[{"id":"2bd6c65512b6f7b3","sum":"B17-B19: typed About values fill only when both asks say the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5; planner asks only named fields; wrongKind needs a host sentence. Heavy lease 2 GiB for swift test. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell (override setters to reformat).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"28beb5cb41b23736","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev scores typed About Name/Email 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; such a value fills only when both asks call it the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16/20, 0 wrong). Planner asks only fields the instruction names; wrongKind needs a host sentence.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0bc8adb9f0371420","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev picks typed About Name/Email at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; prompt rewordings did not help. Such a value fills only when both asks call the field the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16 of 20, 0 wrong).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-ec0243a8194ed7a7","text":"Live Jev picks a typed About Name/Email in both asks but at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 fill cutoff, on standalone forms (B17 held-out: 1-3 of 17 filled, 0 wrong); three prompt rewordings on a dev set did not raise it (evidence/screen/b17/dev).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-3b718a56937eb180","text":"A typed About value fills only when both asks also answer the field's whose-details question as the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (fill.ts); a memory cutoff alone needed 0.6 on B18's dev set and filled 4-7 of 20, the whose question 12 of 20, held-out live 16 of 20 with 0 wrong.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8ece4134d4c0c551","sum":"B18 planner: asks only about fields the instruction names unless asksToFillForm (no field named: nothingToDo); PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind, which v2/host's exhaustive planError switch needs a sentence for.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-c901993f6e9aca54","text":"PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind (B18, kinds.ts misfit: whole address in City, email in Phone); v2/host's AskCaret.planError switch is exhaustive and needs a sentence for it at its next merge of v2/screen.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-d62444babaa7f479","text":"The planner asks only about fields the instruction names (relevance, or namesShortLabel for To/Cc/ID) unless asksToFillForm; an instruction that names no field, like 'msg: ...', now gets nothingToDo (B18 traded that for no unrequested writes).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"94b0d9540949ad9f","sum":"Ask 2 GiB heavy leases for swift test (peaks 0.44 GB). B19 evals: copy new values each time, set offersPerHour and actIfApproved. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell; override cell objectValue/stringValue and accessibilityValue() to reformat.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7a2abedd05327146","sum":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks 0.25-0.44 GB RSS; ask a 2 GiB lease (6 GiB is refused below ~17 GiB free). Routine evals must copy new values each time, or the closed earlier destination's text is credited as the next source and predictions miss (B19).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-db99791d758fef32","text":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks at 0.25-0.44 GB RSS (/usr/bin/time -l, B18); a 6 GiB lease estimate is refused below ~17 GiB free disk, so ask for 2 GiB.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-01ce9c46dd16673e","text":"Routine evals must copy new values each occurrence: with static source text the closed earlier destination's recent text is credited as the next source, the shape changes and predictions miss (B19; caret-fixture --windows forms, stdin form next).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"496e4b113a33f3ef","sum":"B19: real-time skill evals set offersPerHour (Eager 8/h) and writeElsewhere actIfApproved. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell; to reformat, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and accessibilityValue() (setAccessibilityValue never fires).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-69bacc9b74bdc91c","text":"Real-time skill evals need Helper offersPerHour (Eager allows 8 offers an hour) and writeElsewhere set to actIfApproved, since a background-only fixture is never the user's window and ask first caps promotion (B19).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e6e14bbcf17c1b8d","text":"caret-fixture: AX value writes land in the NSTextField's cell and AX reads return a cached value; to reformat input, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and the field's accessibilityValue() -> String? (setAccessibilityValue never fires) (B19).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"69b2a79eea55f5b4","sum":"B19-B21: undoing a skill run resets its clean count; posted clicks reach only a --foreground caret-fixture; pid-posted input resets HIDIdleTime (log last post); a closing window can arrive fieldless; drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for Electron; non-key WKWebView: focusValue.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"22bae55a2a60fd23","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count; a per-pid listen-only tap sees clicks posted to that pid; background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click (use --foreground); pid-posted input resets HIDIdleTime, so GUI evals log their last post.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d9542f01119cf37d","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count. A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid (global monitor and session tap do not); a background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click, --foreground (accessory) does.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e77935deee83e487","text":"Skills (B19): undoing a skill run resets its clean count, so a fixture forced-mismatch run with no Tab needs ten more clean runs after run 11's undo. Live Jev's first naming ask fell under NAME_CUTOFF 0.5 in 7 of 9 tries; the reworded retry picked.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-795f3dcc958c0f2c","text":"A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid; the global NSEvent monitor and a session tap do not (B20, 6 of 6 vs 0 of 6). A background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click and cannot hit-test a covered window; --foreground (accessory) does both.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e619089820dda277","sum":"B20: input posted to a pid resets HIDIdleTime like a person's, so GUI evals record their last post (scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them. TextEdit cannot host a routine: one text area, no positions, one value per field.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T234914Z-993bc2a42fa75599","text":"Input posted to a pid (CGEventPostToPid) resets HIDIdleTime like a person's (B20: 196 s to 0.3 s); GUI evals that post input record their last post (helper/scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them as 'user back'.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-ac2ee9392ce81473","text":"TextEdit cannot host a B19 routine: a shape is (source template, part, destination template) with no positions, a document is one text area, values copied from list lines share one source template, and engine.plan writes one value per field (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f76396784bf60827","sum":"B20-B21: a closing window can reach the model fieldless; routines use last-seen places. Evals starting Electron drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE. A non-key WKWebView writes AXValue to the focused field (reader: focusValue). Shadow keys are hashes, so real-day-replay counts approximate.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a097a19063cce23e","sum":"B20: a closing window can reach the model without its fields before its close, so routines place late edits from where elements were last seen; the agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE, so an eval starting Electron must drop it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-5758654235cf32d7","text":"A closing window (Chrome tearing down its page, a Send that closes it) can reach the model without its fields before its close; routines place late edits and presses from where elements were last seen, or Caret's verified runs score as misses (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T004204Z-584e781bcb96f4a6","text":"The agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for its children; an eval that starts Electron must drop it or Electron runs as plain Node and cannot require('electron') (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"70fc0cfcbac83876","sum":"B20-B21: a non-key WKWebView applies an AXValue write to the focused field, so the reader focuses a web field first (focusValue); the shadow store keeps keys only as hashes, so real-day-replay counts approximate and memory.sqlite routine rows are exact.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-9249ce81a51a9397","text":"WKWebView in a window that is not key applies an AXValue write to whichever field has focus (none: dropped; another: overwritten). The reader focuses a WebKit web field first (focusValue): 3/3 landed, no raise or activation; typing or paste to the pid land 0/3 (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-03e29f7fee084743","text":"The shadow store keeps element keys only as hashes, so an offline replay cannot recover templates or positions; scripts/real-day-replay.ts counts are approximations both ways; memory.sqlite routine rows are the faithful count (B21).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
